// Adjacent to 0904: a second NEGATIVE control. Same past-anchor `since`, but
// here the streak is INTACT (no foreign event) and instead the rigid left
// filter `context.input.amount >= 10` FAILS at the current step (amount = 5).
// Correct verdict: DENY.
//
// This guards against an implementation that, in threading the request
// correlation through the since-anchor branch, drops or mis-scopes the rigid
// `C` filter — which would wrongly PERMIT. Together with 0914 (streak broken)
// this pins both ways the non-vacuous left can legitimately fail, so an
// implementation must reproduce DENY for both while making 0904/0913 PERMIT.
//
// Expected verdicts are in expected_1.out.
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Transfer",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    (Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.user: context.input.user }
        && context.input.amount >= 10)
    since within 1h
    Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.user: "carol" }
};
